load @term/seed/structure/space/vector
  find vector-space

load @term/seed/structure/function/unary
  find unary-function

# A normed vector space: a vector space with a norm, a length assigned to each vector that is zero only for the zero
# vector, scales with scalar multiplication, and obeys the triangle inequality. The norm is exactly the multiplicative
# length the composition algebras carry, and demanding it multiply through the product is the reversibility condition
# that caps the tower at the octonions. The form carries the vector space and the norm; the three norm axioms are the
# laws.
form normed-vector-space
  link space, like vector-space
  link norm, like unary-function
